[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2584973287","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101409#issuecomment-2584973287","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101409","id":2584973287,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aE4_n","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-11T01:04:51Z","updated_at":"2025-01-11T01:05:01Z","body":"We had some debate about whitelisting vs blacklisting the collisions.\r\n\r\nWe mentioned that VRM standard uses whitelisting.\r\n\r\n@lyuma had concerns that inverting the listing would suggest that the less performant option is easier to do.\r\n\r\nTokage is ok with either but proposed blacklisting.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2584973287/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2584985732","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101409#issuecomment-2584985732","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101409","id":2584985732,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aE8CE","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-11T01:31:10Z","updated_at":"2025-01-11T01:37:37Z","body":"If we are concerned about performance, this is not much of a basis for concern, since we need to be careful when using either list.\r\n\r\nThe most serious problem is that without allow list, you cannot control the order in which collisions are handled on a per-bone chain basis, which could break strict compatibility with VRM. So support for permission lists is a must.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6cd25b9d-cb83-4a0b-92bb-8c7114d7f56a\r\n\r\nHowever, I believe it is necessary for quality of life, because when using exclusion lists, the user's operation steps when creating a mockup are cut in half or less.\r\n\r\nFor example, the following case:\r\n\r\n1. There are 4 bone chains, 5 normal collisions, and 1 inside collider.\r\n2. Apply the 5 normal collisions to all bone chains.\r\n3. I want to apply the inside collider to only one bone chain. However, I need to exclude the inside collider from the other 3 bone chains.\r\n\r\nIn this case, the allow list would require `4*5+1=21` steps, whereas the exclude list would only require `3*1=3` steps.\r\n\r\nHowever, in the case where 5 normal collisions are not applied to all bone chains (so if step 2 is not needed), the allow list requires fewer steps.\r\n\r\nSo it is a matter of which direction to go in to the destination state, and I thought both should be supported. For now, it resets when the allow/exclude list is switched, but I think we can send follow up PR with an option to invert the list in the future if there are demands.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2584985732/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585557894","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101409#issuecomment-2585557894","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101409","id":2585557894,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aHHuG","user":{"login":"ettiSurreal","id":98223724,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdrGbA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98223724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal","html_url":"https://github.com/ettiSurreal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ettiSurreal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-12T03:06:54Z","updated_at":"2025-01-12T03:06:54Z","body":"I think `drag` should be called `damp` to align with the physics nodes. \r\n`value` could also be called something else, I'm guessing it's called such because `influence` is already used by SkeletonModifier3D, so maybe something like `factor` or `weight` could work?\r\n\r\nThe documentation could also mention that if you need an equivalent to this that interacts with physics bodies you can use Generic6DOFJoint3D angular spring stiffness on a PhysicalBone3D (at least when Jolt is used).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585557894/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585558910","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101409#issuecomment-2585558910","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101409","id":2585558910,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aHH9-","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-12T03:11:49Z","updated_at":"2025-01-12T04:18:27Z","body":"@ettiSurreal Since this is not a physical node, consistency with the physical node is not very important; rather, it is more appropriate to follow the VRM naming convention since VRMSpringBone is a cross-platform module. Also, we will not write a reference to 6DOFJoint3D since the SpringBoneSimulator process is completely different from that of physical nodes, and the consistency of their behavior should never be guaranteed. This is why we write at the beginning of the document that it has no relation to PhysicalServer.\r\n\r\nBTW, damp is a value that represents scaling, and its meaning is strictly different from that of drag which represents resistivity. In other words, damp is multiplicative and drag is subtractive.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe property name “value” may be too generic, but at least the word \"value\" is commonly used in arguments, so I think it is not a problem. Because of the need to have a hierarchy for grouping, it is necessary to have the name “value” to indicate that it is the value of the hierarchy itself, instead of an anonymous name. Also, when using it in code, it is always in the form of a path with \"/\" like \"radius/value\", \"gravity/value\", so I believe which is not a problem. Then \"influence\", \"factor\" and \"weight\". are not appropriate in view of the implications and consistency.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585558910/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585835359","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101409#issuecomment-2585835359","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101409","id":2585835359,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aILdf","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-12T17:03:31Z","updated_at":"2025-01-12T17:05:45Z","body":"I've been reviewing it in https://github.com/V-Sekai/godot-vrm/issues/119\r\n\r\nhttps://youtu.be/0XLIFrK3SSQ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585835359/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2585844812","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101409#issuecomment-2585844812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101409","id":2585844812,"node_id":"IC_k